## 1. Purpose

This repository contains proprietary assets, workflows, templates, documentation, automation systems, editorial guidelines, and intellectual property developed and maintained by the CSE Newsletter Committee, Department of Computer Science & Engineering, Pandit Deendayal Energy University (PDEU).

This repository is intended solely for the internal operations of the CSE Newsletter Committee.

No part of this repository is considered open-source software.

---

## 2. Ownership

All rights, titles, and interests in the following materials remain the exclusive property of the CSE Newsletter Committee:

* HTML Templates
* Newsletter Designs
* Editorial Workflows
* Claude Project Instructions
* AI Automation Systems
* Branding Assets
* Logos
* Graphics
* Icons
* Documentation
* Source Code
* Repository Structure
* Generated Content Frameworks
* Internal Processes

The inclusion of materials in this repository does not grant ownership rights to any contributor, committee member, or third party.

---

## 3. Restrictions

Without prior written authorization from the Committee Leadership, users shall NOT:

### 3.1 Redistribution

* Share repository contents externally
* Upload repository contents to public platforms
* Publish repository files on GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, or similar services
* Distribute copies to non-members

### 3.2 Commercial Use

* Sell repository contents
* License repository contents
* Monetize repository assets
* Use repository materials for commercial consulting or services

### 3.3 Derivative Projects

* Create competing versions
* Republish workflows under another organization
* Rebrand repository materials
* Remove ownership notices

### 3.4 Asset Extraction

* Copy templates for external organizations
* Reuse committee branding externally
* Reuse repository assets without authorization

---

## 4. Modification Policy

Repository modifications are permitted only under the following conditions:

### Minor Updates

Examples:

* Bug fixes
* Typographical corrections
* Documentation improvements

These may be proposed through approved committee workflows.

### Major Updates

Examples:

* Template redesigns
* Workflow changes
* Automation modifications
* Structural repository changes
* Branding updates
* Design system updates

Require approval from:

* Heads OR Newsletter Committee Leadership

before implementation.

Unauthorized modifications are prohibited.

---

## 5. Confidentiality

Repository contents are considered internal operational resources of the CSE Newsletter Committee.

Members must treat all repository materials as confidential unless explicitly approved for public release.

This includes:

* Templates
* Prompts
* Workflows
* Internal documentation
* Automation systems
* Design assets

---

## 6. Contributor Responsibilities

Contributors must:

* Preserve repository integrity
* Maintain ownership notices
* Respect committee branding guidelines
* Follow approval workflows
* Avoid unauthorized disclosure

Contributors do not acquire ownership of repository intellectual property through contributions.

All accepted contributions become part of the repository and remain the property of the CSE Newsletter Committee.

